  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": 2,
      "issue_number": 6165,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "The Werkzeug docs were updated to say what they say now [approximately a month ago](https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug/pull/3251). I don't constantly go back and forth keeping the two in sync.\n\n`MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH` should not be _avoided_. In fact, the docs as written in Werkzeug wouldn't help you either. They say that `max_content_length` must be set _somewhere_. The problem you're reporting is that Waitress buffers the response before it gets to the application. Because of that Waitress behavior, the max length can only be configured there, not further down the stack.\n\nSo I suppose what the docs need to say is \"be aware of the stack you're using, how each tool interacts with requests and responses, and how to configure each one appropriately.\" That seems like such general advice, and applies to everything not just `max_content_length`, so I don't think it's worth saying specifically there.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/6165#issuecomment-5838756975",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/6165",
      "actor_login": "davidism",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-09-25T20:02:27"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "issue_number": 6165,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "That has nothing to do with Flask, you need to configure Waitress, or the HTTP server in front of Waitress.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/6165#issuecomment-5823580011",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/6165",
      "actor_login": "davidism",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-09-24T22:56:18"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "issue_number": 6146,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "It looks like the examples repo listed at the bottom of that page doesn't actually include the referenced example.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/6146#issuecomment-5483308783",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/6146",
      "actor_login": "davidism",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-08-31T19:20:33"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "issue_number": 6143,
      "pr_number": null,
